- Prevent debugging statements in production
- Validate dependencies regularly
- Follow conventional commit standards
- Automate quality checks completely
- Fail fast on quality issues

## Lefthook Quality Integration

- Pre-commit quality gates @lefthook.yml
- Automated formatting enforcement
- Static analysis validation
- Debug statement prevention
- Dependency health checks
- Conventional commit validation
- Fast feedback on quality issues

```yaml
# Lefthook pre-commit configuration
pre-commit:
  parallel: true
  commands:
    dart-format:
      tags: quality
      glob: "**/*.dart"
      run: flutter format {staged_files} && git add {staged_files}
      stage_fixed: true

    dart-analyze:
      tags: quality
      run: flutter analyze --fatal-infos --fatal-warnings
```

## Code Formatting Standards

- Use `flutter format` exclusively
- Auto-format on pre-commit
- 80-character line length limit
- Consistent indentation with spaces
- Trailing comma for collections
- Import organization automatically
- No manual formatting overrides

## Static Analysis Rules

- Enable all lint rules @analysis_options.yaml
- Treat warnings as errors
- No analyzer suppressions allowed
- Custom lint rules enabled
- Performance lint rules active
- Security lint rules enforced
- Documentation lint rules required

```yaml
# analysis_options.yaml configuration
include: package:flutter_lints/flutter.yaml

analyzer:
  errors:
    invalid_annotation_target: ignore
  exclude:
    - "**/*.g.dart"
    - "**/*.freezed.dart"

linter:
  rules:
    prefer_const_constructors: true
    prefer_const_declarations: true
    avoid_print: true
```

## Debug Statement Prevention

- No `print()` statements in lib/
- No `debugPrint()` statements in lib/
- Use proper logging framework
- Remove console.log equivalents
- Prevent debug imports
- Use logging package instead
- Catch debug statements pre-commit

```bash
# Debug statement detection
if grep -r "print(" lib/ --include="*.dart" 2>/dev/null; then
  echo "❌ Found print() statements in lib/"
  echo "💡 Use logging framework instead"
  exit 1
fi
```

